      <li><span class="sym">⚷</span><strong>Chiron</strong><em>1977</em><span class="sym-meta">a centaur between ♄ and ♅; read as the durable wound</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⚸</span><strong>Black Moon Lilith</strong><em>—</em><span class="sym-meta">the empty focus of the lunar ellipse, not a body at all</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⚳</span><strong>Ceres</strong><em>1801</em><span class="sym-meta">first asteroid found, now a dwarf planet; nourishment</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⚴</span><strong>Pallas</strong><em>1802</em><span class="sym-meta">strategy and pattern recognition</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⚵</span><strong>Juno</strong><em>1804</em><span class="sym-meta">contract, partnership, the terms of a bond</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⚶</span><strong>Vesta</strong><em>1807</em><span class="sym-meta">devotion, the tended fire, what you keep alight</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⊗</span><strong>Part of Fortune</strong><em>Pars Fortunae</em><span class="sym-meta">a calculated point, not an object: Asc + ☽ − ☉</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted small">Note what the list records: a tradition that absorbed ♅, ♆, ♇ and ⚷ after the
    telescope found them, and assigned meanings afterwards. No astrologer predicted a planet before an
    astronomer saw it. <span class="sci">◆ Established</span>, and it is the most awkward fact in the craft.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="frame reveal">
    <p class="kicker">ANGLES, ASPECTS AND THE WORKING MARKS <span class="hist">◆</span></p>
    <ul class="sym-grid sym-grid--tight">
      <li><span class="sym">☌</span><strong>Conjunction</strong><span class="sym-meta">0° · fused, for better and worse</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">☍</span><strong>Opposition</strong><span class="sym-meta">180° · facing, aware, pulled apart</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">△</span><strong>Trine</strong><span class="sym-meta">120° · easy, same element, lazy if unworked</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">□</span><strong>Square</strong><span class="sym-meta">90° · friction, and therefore movement</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⚹</span><strong>Sextile</strong><span class="sym-meta">60° · opportunity you have to take up</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⚺</span><strong>Semisextile</strong><span class="sym-meta">30° · minor, uneasy neighbours</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⚻</span><strong>Quincunx</strong><span class="sym-meta">150° · no shared element, no common language</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">⚼</span><strong>Sesquiquadrate</strong><span class="sym-meta">135° · Kepler's addition, agitation</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">∠</span><strong>Semisquare</strong><span class="sym-meta">45° · the small persistent irritation</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">Asc</span><strong>Ascendant</strong><span class="sym-meta">the ecliptic degree rising in the east</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">Dsc</span><strong>Descendant</strong><span class="sym-meta">opposite the Ascendant; the met other</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">MC</span><strong>Midheaven</strong><span class="sym-meta">medium coeli · vocation, the public shape</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">IC</span><strong>Imum Coeli</strong><span class="sym-meta">the root, the home, the buried floor</span></li>
      <li><span class="sym">℞</span><strong>Retrograde</strong><span class="sym-meta">apparent backward motion — a parallax effect, not a force</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted small">Retrograde is worth dwelling on. Nothing reverses: ℞ is what it looks like when
    the Earth overtakes an outer planet on the inside lane. The appearance is real and entirely explained.
    <span class="sci">◆ Established.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <p class="kicker">THE FOUR ELEMENTS <span class="myth">◆</span></p>
      <ul class="sym-grid sym-grid--wide">
        <li><span class="sym">🜂</span><strong>Fire</strong><span class="sym-meta">♈ ♌ ♐ · ignition, will, the thing that starts</span></li>
        <li><span class="sym">🜃</span><strong>Earth</strong><span class="sym-meta">♉ ♍ ♑ · substance, maintenance, the thing that lasts</span></li>
        <li><span class="sym">🜁</span><strong>Air</strong><span class="sym-meta">♊ ♎ ♒ · relation, speech, the thing that connects</span></li>
        <li><span class="sym">🜄</span><strong>Water</strong><span class="sym-meta">♋ ♏ ♓ · feeling, memory, the thing that dissolves</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted small">The same four triangles are the alchemical signs — see
      <a href="/elemental-alchemy/">Limb X</a>, where they are read as states and tendencies rather than
      substances.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <p class="kicker">THE THREE MODES <span class="myth">◆</span></p>
      <ul class="sym-grid sym-grid--wide">
        <li><span class="sym">◑</span><strong>Cardinal</strong><span class="sym-meta">♈ ♋ ♎ ♑ · the four season-openers; initiation</span></li>
        <li><span class="sym">■</span><strong>Fixed</strong><span class="sym-meta">♉ ♌ ♏ ♒ · mid-season; consolidation and stubbornness</span></li>
        <li><span class="sym">◇</span><strong>Mutable</strong><span class="sym-meta">♊ ♍ ♐ ♓ · season's end; adaptation and dispersal</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted small">Four elements times three modes gives exactly twelve combinations, each used
      once. That tidiness is the real engine of the system — and a clue that it is a classification scheme
      rather than an observation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

