<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <h2>Where This Order Stands</h2>
    <p>Astrology does not work as a physical theory, and the order will not soften that to keep anyone
    comfortable. The tests were fair, some were designed with astrologers' agreement, and they failed.</p>
    <p>And: it is the longest-running attempt humans have made to read meaning into time, it invented the
    observational rigour that eventually refuted it, and it preserves a vocabulary of temperament and season
    that our own age is conspicuously poorer for lacking. Kepler kept casting charts while despising the
    practice of his contemporaries, and he was not a fool.</p>
    <p>Use it as a mirror and it is a fine instrument. Use it as a forecast and it will quietly take your
    agency away. The sky is not writing about you — but four thousand years of people watching it very
    carefully is a library, and we are not in the business of burning libraries.</p>
    <p class="mt-1"><a class="btn" href="/ask-ed/">Put a question to Ed</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
